ut_data,\n    result=extension_manager.result,\n    errors=extension_manager.to_array(),\n    exit_code=1\n)\n```\n\n### 3. Cancellation Flag\n\n**Set in extension_cancel():**\n\n```python\ndef extension_cancel(self):\n    extension_manager.set_cancelled()\n```\n\n**Check in actions:**\n\n```python\nfor item in items:\n    if extension_manager.is_cancelled():\n        raise OperationCancelledError(\"User cancelled\")\n    process(item)\n```\n\n## Methods\n\n**`clear()`** - Reset all state (call at extension start)\n\n**`add_error(exception, **kwargs)`** - Add error with context\n\n**`set_result(result)`** - Store partial result data\n\n**`has_errors()`** - Check if any errors collected\n\n**`error_count()`** - Get count of errors\n\n**`to_array()`** - Get errors as list for unv_output\n\n**`result`** - Property to get result data\n\n**`errors`** - Property to get errors list\n\n**`set_cancelled()`** - Set cancellation flag\n\n**`is_cancelled()`** - Check if cancelled\n\n**`cancelled`** - Property for cancellation status\n\n**`set_uac_variables(variables: dict)`** - Store UAC variables dict (call once at extension start)\n\n**`uac_variables`** - Property returning the UAC variables dict; returns `{}` if not set\n\n### 4. UAC Variables\n\nUAC variables are set once during extension initialisation and accessed by any action that needs them.\n\n**Set during extension startup (in `extension.py`):**\n\n```python\nextension_manager.set_uac_variables(self.uip.task_variables)\n```\n\n**Access in actions:**\n\n```python\nextension_manager = ExtensionManager()\n\ndef my_action(input_data: InputFields) -> ActionOutput:\n    uac_vars = extension_manager.uac_variables\n    task_instance_id = uac_vars.get(\"taskInstanceId\", \"\")\n    my_variable = uac_vars.get(\"MY_UAC_VARIABLE\", \"\")\n    ...\n```\n\n`uac_variables` returns an empty dict `{}` if not set — actions can safely call `.get()` without guards.\n\n---\n\n## Singleton Pattern\n\nExtensionManager uses singleton pattern - same instance accessed everywhere:\n\n```python\nfrom manager import ExtensionManager\nextension_manager = ExtensionManager()  # Same instance\n```\n\nSee src/manager.py for full implementation.","numLines":140,"startLine":1,"totalLines":140}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LiXReerKXVLeXgjmhJu8J4","duration_ms":2}

